While many obvious problems have been fixed with the emperor edition (ages later) the game still doesn't have the integrity of the previous total war games. the campaign map has been stripped of everything that made it enjoyable and the battles are still clunky, buggy, and overall poorly made, not to mention naval battles have never been good in the total war series. furthermore this game requires a pretty good pc just to get an enjoyable framerate with meagre graphics. i have 4GB of ram a 6770hd graphics card and an i5 processor and i get 30fps with all the graphics settings at bare bone, including small unit sizes. in shogun 2 i could run the game at ultra settings and field over 5,000 units on screen at once and get 40-55 fps.
if you really like the period that this game is based off of, wait until the price goes down to around $40 or less and don't buy any of the culture packs (most of the content is already in the game and the factions are not even enjoyable)
if you really want a good modern total war game purchase shogun 2, the 2 main dlc campaigns add 2 completely new time periods and the clans all have very unique attributes that make them fresh and interesting.

